{"duration_api_ms":186994,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"77321d2b-112b-47ba-a19b-0cd57e3621ab","total_cost_usd":0.6667438000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":84,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34360,"cache_read_input_tokens":1999879,"output_tokens":12916,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2103},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34360,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1856,"cache_read_input_tokens":58041,"cache_creation_input_tokens":650,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":650},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":84,"outputTokens":12916,"cacheReadInputTokens":1999879,"cacheCreationInputTokens":34360,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6667438000000001,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":2103,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":43,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"On node1 (Alpine 3.23), set up nginx serving HTTPS on port 8443 with a self-signed cert (5-min validity for demonstration) that is auto-renewed by a busybox cron job (every minute, renews when <2min of validity remain) via /usr/local/bin/renew-cert.sh, which atomically replaces cert/key and gracefully reloads nginx (`rc-service nginx reload`) so it picks up the new cert without dropping requests. Verified two live renewals with a continuous HTTPS probe loop showing 100% 200 responses across the cert swap, confirmed both nginx and crond are enabled at boot, restarted node1, confirmed changed boot_id, and confirmed HTTPS plus a third automatic renewal succeeded post-reboot.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed nginx, openssl, busybox-openrc, curl on node1 via apk\",\"Created /usr/local/bin/renew-cert.sh: checks cert expiry with openssl x509 -checkend, generates a new 5-minute self-signed cert atomically, logs to /var/log/certrenew/renew.log, and reloads nginx gracefully\",\"Configured /etc/nginx/http.d/ssl-8443.conf to serve HTTPS on 0.0.0.0:8443 using /etc/nginx/ssl/cert.pem and key.pem\",\"Enabled and started nginx (rc-update add nginx default; rc-service nginx start)\",\"Installed a root crontab entry running renew-cert.sh every minute and enabled/started crond\",\"Ran a continuous curl+openssl monitoring loop against $NODE_IP:8443 for ~4.5 minutes to observe a live renewal with zero downtime (68/68 probes returned 200, serial changed mid-loop)\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, uptime, service status, HTTPS 200, cert serial/dates)\",\"Restarted node1 with `reboot` (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)\",\"Polled node1 until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed and uptime -s reflects new boot time\",\"Verified nginx and crond auto-started at boot and are enabled in the default runlevel\",\"Confirmed HTTPS still serving 200 post-reboot and waited for a fresh automatic cert renewal to occur, confirming the full renew+reload pipeline persists after restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"HTTPS served on port 8443 with a certificate\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5bbce8a7f51a46d0\",\"cmd-92a6e132965542c3\",\"cmd-2a881b3348334786\"],\"summary\":\"nginx config validated, started, listening on 0.0.0.0:8443, curl returns 200 and TLS cert served with matching serial/dates\"},{\"requirement\":\"Certificate renewed automatically before expiry\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7317d606148b4a19\",\"cmd-01315c2377c144b7\",\"cmd-2813f19c99b54003\"],\"summary\":\"crond installed with per-minute renewal job; renew.log shows automatic renewal at 09:51:00 (serial changed from 21B27... to 1F57AFC...) without manual intervention\"},{\"requirement\":\"Service picks up new certificate while continuing to answer requests (no downtime)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2813f19c99b54003\",\"cmd-fe124194a51b4a04\"],\"summary\":\"Continuous monitor loop across the renewal boundary recorded 68/68 HTTP 200 responses with the serving cert serial switching mid-loop, proving graceful nginx reload with zero dropped requests\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e13a74cb61344868\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 0ede1030..., nginx/crond status started, HTTPS 200, and current cert serial/dates prior to reboot\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-26292a39b1404a0a\",\"cmd-a262deadc7db4c58\",\"cmd-c730ef41cfbd45d8\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot command acknowledged before disconnect; node1 became unreachable then responded again; boot_id changed to 0cc37d0c... (new value) and uptime -s reflects a fresh boot time\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery of required services and data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c730ef41cfbd45d8\",\"cmd-c8da05efa4524cfa\",\"cmd-bd2f0de0779e4847\"],\"summary\":\"nginx and crond auto-started and enabled at boot; HTTPS returns 200 post-reboot; a further automatic cert renewal (serial 62CB58C8...) occurred via cron after the restart, confirming the renewal pipeline survives a reboot\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"On node1 (Alpine 3.23), set up nginx serving HTTPS on port 8443 with a self-signed cert (5-min validity for demonstration) that is auto-renewed by a busybox cron job (every minute, renews when <2min of validity remain) via /usr/local/bin/renew-cert.sh, which atomically replaces cert/key and gracefully reloads nginx (`rc-service nginx reload`) so it picks up the new cert without dropping requests. Verified two live renewals with a continuous HTTPS probe loop showing 100% 200 responses across the cert swap, confirmed both nginx and crond are enabled at boot, restarted node1, confirmed changed boot_id, and confirmed HTTPS plus a third automatic renewal succeeded post-reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed nginx, openssl, busybox-openrc, curl on node1 via apk","Created /usr/local/bin/renew-cert.sh: checks cert expiry with openssl x509 -checkend, generates a new 5-minute self-signed cert atomically, logs to /var/log/certrenew/renew.log, and reloads nginx gracefully","Configured /etc/nginx/http.d/ssl-8443.conf to serve HTTPS on 0.0.0.0:8443 using /etc/nginx/ssl/cert.pem and key.pem","Enabled and started nginx (rc-update add nginx default; rc-service nginx start)","Installed a root crontab entry running renew-cert.sh every minute and enabled/started crond","Ran a continuous curl+openssl monitoring loop against $NODE_IP:8443 for ~4.5 minutes to observe a live renewal with zero downtime (68/68 probes returned 200, serial changed mid-loop)","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, uptime, service status, HTTPS 200, cert serial/dates)","Restarted node1 with `reboot` (backgrounded so the ack returned before disconnect)","Polled node1 until exec was available again, confirmed boot_id changed and uptime -s reflects new boot time","Verified nginx and crond auto-started at boot and are enabled in the default runlevel","Confirmed HTTPS still serving 200 post-reboot and waited for a fresh automatic cert renewal to occur, confirming the full renew+reload pipeline persists after restart"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"HTTPS served on port 8443 with a certificate","command_ids":["cmd-5bbce8a7f51a46d0","cmd-92a6e132965542c3","cmd-2a881b3348334786"],"summary":"nginx config validated, started, listening on 0.0.0.0:8443, curl returns 200 and TLS cert served with matching serial/dates"},{"requirement":"Certificate renewed automatically before expiry","command_ids":["cmd-7317d606148b4a19","cmd-01315c2377c144b7","cmd-2813f19c99b54003"],"summary":"crond installed with per-minute renewal job; renew.log shows automatic renewal at 09:51:00 (serial changed from 21B27... to 1F57AFC...) without manual intervention"},{"requirement":"Service picks up new certificate while continuing to answer requests (no downtime)","command_ids":["cmd-2813f19c99b54003","cmd-fe124194a51b4a04"],"summary":"Continuous monitor loop across the renewal boundary recorded 68/68 HTTP 200 responses with the serving cert serial switching mid-loop, proving graceful nginx reload with zero dropped requests"},{"requirement":"node1 healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-e13a74cb61344868"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 0ede1030..., nginx/crond status started, HTTPS 200, and current cert serial/dates prior to reboot"},{"requirement":"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-26292a39b1404a0a","cmd-a262deadc7db4c58","cmd-c730ef41cfbd45d8"],"summary":"Reboot command acknowledged before disconnect; node1 became unreachable then responded again; boot_id changed to 0cc37d0c... (new value) and uptime -s reflects a fresh boot time"},{"requirement":"node1 post-restart recovery of required services and data","command_ids":["cmd-c730ef41cfbd45d8","cmd-c8da05efa4524cfa","cmd-bd2f0de0779e4847"],"summary":"nginx and crond auto-started and enabled at boot; HTTPS returns 200 post-reboot; a further automatic cert renewal (serial 62CB58C8...) occurred via cron after the restart, confirming the renewal pipeline survives a reboot"}]},"ttft_ms":5117,"type":"result","duration_ms":499355,"uuid":"c78a155b-3ef2-44b6-9ca8-0be3bed508ef","ttft_stream_ms":2410,"time_to_request_ms":63,"first_content_frame_ms":2411,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
